  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Mahgeetah** (1 review): Show opens spectacularly with Mahgeetah and Dancefloors, featuring new It Still Moves tracks [5]\n- **Phone Went West** (1 review): Reviewer highlights the acoustic tunes and the massive Phone Went West performance [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **I Still Miss Someone**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2003-09-26.shnf** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 120 min; rated 4.6/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: Drums are excessively loud, drowning out guitar and vocals during intense passages; High energy performance with a nice sound, typical of audience recordings [2][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Considered a benchmark moment, representing the band well during early It Still Moves touring [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2003-09-26.shnf**: taped by Jon Ice; transferred by Jon Ice; source: AKG ck63 > Active Cables > JK LABS DVC > Canare Starquad Interconnects > Apogee Mini Me (line in) > M1 @ 48k [1]",
